.TH WMMEDIA 1 "2026" "wmmedia 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmmedia \- Window Maker dockapp for controlling a media player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmmedia
[\fB\-display\fR \fIDPY\fR] [\fB\-w\fR] [\fB\-b\fR \fIBACKEND\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPLAYER\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-r\fR] [\fB\-fg\fR \fIRRGGBB\fR] [\fB\-t\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A 64x64 dock tile in the style of wmvol: three black bevelled LCD boxes showing a state icon,
the elapsed (or remaining) time, scrolling title and artist lines, previous / play-pause / next
keys and a progress bar. Window Maker's own dock-tile texture shows around the boxes.
The player is controlled by running
\fBplayerctl\fR(1) (any MPRIS player) or \fBmpc\fR(1) (MPD).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-display " DPY"
X display to use.
.TP
.B \-w
Run in a normal window instead of docking (preview only; without this option the tile is a dockapp).
.TP
.BI \-b " BACKEND"
\fBplayerctl\fR (default) or \fBmpc\fR.
.TP
.BI \-p " PLAYER"
Player name passed to \fBplayerctl \-p\fR (for example \fBspotify\fR or \fBmpv\fR).
By default playerctl picks the first player it finds.
.TP
.BI \-s " N"
Mouse-wheel volume step in percent, 1\-50 (default 5).
.TP
.B \-r
Show the remaining time instead of the elapsed time (clicking the time toggles it).
.TP
.BI \-fg " RRGGBB"
LCD colour (default 20b2aa, the wmvol teal). Always wins over \fB\-t\fR.
.TP
.B \-t
Take the LCD colour from the Window Maker theme instead of using the fixed teal.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE"
Window Maker defaults file read by \fB\-t\fR
(default \fB~/GNUstep/Defaults/WindowMaker\fR).
.TP
.B \-notheme
Accepted for compatibility with 1.x; this is now the default.
.TP
.BI \-D " PREFIX"
Debug: write PREFIX\-tile.ppm after the first poll and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-v
Help, version.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
Left click on a key
Previous / play-pause / next (fires on release; drag off the key to cancel).
.TP
Left click or drag on the progress bar
Seek. While dragging the time box shows the target; one seek is sent on release.
.TP
Left click on the time
Toggle elapsed / remaining time.
.TP
Wheel
Volume up/down by the step. Shift+wheel changes it by 1%. The volume is shown for 1.5 s.
.TP
Middle click
Stop.
.PP
The keys, wheel and bar do nothing while no player is running. Hold the window manager modifier
to drag the tile inside the dock.
.SH THEME
With \fB\-t\fR the LCD colours are derived from the colours of the active Window Maker theme, read from
\fB~/GNUstep/Defaults/WindowMaker\fR and re-checked about once a second, so applying a theme
recolours the tile without a restart.
.SH FILES AND ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ~/GNUstep/Defaults/WindowMaker
Theme source for \fB\-t\fR. The player commands are found through \fBPATH\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR playerctl (1),
.BR mpc (1),
.BR wmaker (1)
